extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the text-layer cache (p031-p033) and checked against 150 dpi
    renders of cache p031-p033 (printed 30-32).
  - The id is squire-of-the-white-rose because `squire` is the Palladium
    Fantasy class.
  - The ten specialties are stored in skills.mos with choose 1. The book lets
    a Squire take TWO specialties by dropping its other O.C.C. Skills, keeping
    only Hand to Hand and the W.P.s; that trade is not stored and is in the body.
    Note the book says "Hand to Hand: Martial Arts" in that sentence while the
    Squire''s O.C.C. skill is Expert, changeable to Martial Arts.
  - The O.C.C. bonuses "+1D4 to P.S. or P.E." and "+1 to P.P. or M.A." are
    stored as two ability choice groups, each option carrying its bonus. The
    rest of the bonus block is stored as printed; pull punch is +1 at level 1
    and at 4, 8, 12 and 15, initiative +1 at 2, 6 and 12.
  - Mechanic MOS "Locksmith (+10%) or Salvage (+15%)" stores no bonus, as the
    Merc Soldier''s Transportation MOS does for the same shape.
  - Lore Master "Five Lore skills of choice" is a named list of every Rifts
    Lore row in the catalog, Cowboy''s two included.
  - Pilot MOS "four piloting skills, not robot or power armor" and the related
    Pilot exclusions: the MOS group opens the whole Pilot category with the
    exclusion in its note; the related-skill list names the excluded rows.
    "Aircraft" is read as Airplane, Jet Aircraft and Helicopter plus the
    military aircraft rows.
  - The silver dagger is stored as knife-silver-plated, the catalog''s nearest
    row. Three weeks of rations is one food-rations entry; 50 feet of strong
    cord/rope is one cord entry.
  - Not in equipment_starting, left to the body: one weapon per W.P. with
    1D4+2 E-Clips, Squire armor or other light-medium armor (the book
    names no specific suit), the M.D.C. barding, and the Pilot MOS vehicles.
    The White Rose kit is stored: two petals, three leaves, one healing potion.
  - Starting money stores the 1D4x100 credits; the 3D6x100 in tradable
    artifacts is barter goods and stays in the body.
  - occ_group is men-of-arms, from the book''s own "other Men at Arms" on
    printed 30. The class states no S.D.C. base beyond the +10 bonus, so it
    needs a CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS entry (3D6).
  - Language: American and Literacy: American are stored as one pick from the
    repeatable Language: Other / Literacy: Other rows with the printed bonus,
    so the player names the language American. The catalog has no row for
    either, and a stub would be a wrong zero-percent row.
  - Experience table: printed 79, "Squire O.C.C. of the White Rose".
---

## Lore

Many who want to fight evil and oppose the Mystic Knights lack the psionic and
magical gifts a White Knight needs. Those with a warrior''s heart can still join
the Order of the White Rose as Squires and ride alongside a Knight.

A Squire is not an apprentice and never becomes a Knight, not being a Mystic.
Squires are heroes and support specialists in their own right, with solid
combat training and a specialty - often communications, mechanics, medicine or
technical work - that covers what a combat-focused Knight lacks. About 65% of
Knights actively want one to four Squires on their team and treat them as
technical officers. Squires keep the same code as the Knights, are trusted with
the Order''s secrets, and fight fiercely beside their partner.

Candidates are sought out one at a time for character, loyalty, courage and
skill. A third are D-Bees and a tenth are Haven Mutants. A Squire always treats
the Knight he serves with as the team leader.

## Two Specialties

The book allows a Squire to take two MOS instead of one. The price is every other
O.C.C. Skill: only Hand to Hand and the W.P.s are kept. The app offers one specialty;
a player taking two should agree the swap with the G.M. and drop the other
O.C.C. Skills by hand.

## Equipment and Money

Beyond the kit listed in the class, a Squire has one weapon for each W.P. with
1D4+2 spare E-Clips (TW or other magic weapons only with G.M. approval), and
Squire armor or another light to medium suit, not environmental.

Magic healing: two White Rose petals, three White Rose leaves and one healing
potion, with more issued for special missions.

Transportation: usually a horse in M.D.C. barding. A Squire with the Pilot MOS
instead starts with a car and one other vehicle he is skilled in. The Order may
provide other vehicles on assignment.

Money: 1D4x100 credits plus 3D6x100 credits'' worth of tradable artifacts.
Squires prefer barter to leave no money trail.

## GM Notes

About 662 Squires serve the Order, half of them away at any time.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'squire-of-the-white-rose');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'squire-of-the-white-rose';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-squire-of-the-white-rose-class.sql');
